-   entry .Error   raised when text is not a valid semantic version
+   entry .Error   ausgelöst, wenn Text keine gültige semantische Version ist

=   entry .Error   raised when text is not a valid semantic version
-     detail
+     detail

-         Error `↯/s.97.1`: _`version` is not a valid semantic version because …_, with one of four
-         reasons: `BadFormat` (_the string did not match the SemVer 2.0 grammar_, such as
-         `1.2` or `1.2.3.4`), `EmptyIdentifier` (_a prerelease or build identifier was
-         empty_, as in `1.2.3-`), `LeadingZero` (_a numeric identifier had a leading zero_,
-         as in `01.1.1` or `1.2.3-0123`) and `InvalidCharacter` (_an identifier contained a
-         character outside `[0-9A-Za-z-]`_). Raised by `Semver.decodable`; a `v"…"` literal
-         reports the same problems as a compile error instead.
-     entry .Reason   why text is not a semantic version: bad format, an empty identifier, a leading zero or a bad character
+         Fehler `↯/s.97.1`: _`version` is not a valid semantic version because …_, mit einem von
+         vier Gründen: `BadFormat` (_the string did not match the SemVer 2.0 grammar_, etwa
+         `1.2` oder `1.2.3.4`), `EmptyIdentifier` (_a prerelease or build identifier was
+         empty_, wie in `1.2.3-`), `LeadingZero` (_a numeric identifier had a leading zero_,
+         wie in `01.1.1` oder `1.2.3-0123`) und `InvalidCharacter` (_an identifier contained a
+         character outside `[0-9A-Za-z-]`_). Ausgelöst von `Semver.decodable`; ein
+         `v"…"`-Literal meldet dieselben Probleme stattdessen als Kompilierfehler.
+     entry .Reason   warum Text keine semantische Version ist: falsches Format, ein leerer Bezeichner, eine führende Null oder ein ungültiges Zeichen

-       detail
+       detail

